.TH DWARFSCTL 1 "2026-11-14" "dwarfsctl 0.13.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dwarfsctl \- JSON backend and KDE integration for DwarFS images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dwarfsctl
.RI [ --config " FILE"]
.RB [ --verbose ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Build, inspect, browse, mount and extract read-only DwarFS images.
Every command emits a JSON envelope on standard output. Diagnostics go to
standard error. There is no --json switch.
Mount control uses the tray's session D-Bus service; other operations work
without a desktop session. This is an unofficial integration, not affiliated
with the DwarFS project.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " FILE"
Merge this configuration after system and user configuration.
.TP
.B --verbose
Increase diagnostics on standard error.
.TP
.B --help
Show global help; use COMMAND --help for command arguments.
.TP
.B --version
Show version and affiliation notice.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS build
.B build SRC_DIR --output IMAGE
.RB [ --force ]
.RB [ --overwrite-output ]
.RB [ --yes ]
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.RI [ --compression " ALGO"]
.RI [ --mkdwarfs-arg " TOKEN"]
.PP
Create an image using the bundled engine. --force permits replacement and
enables replacement in the engine. --overwrite-output bypasses the backend overwrite
prompt; --yes answers that prompt affirmatively. --dry-run reports the plan
without executing it. Repeat --mkdwarfs-arg for individual argv tokens;
input/output options are owned by dwarfsctl. --compress aliases --compression.
.SS mount
.B mount IMAGE
.PP
Mount through the session D-Bus tray agent.
.SS mount list
.B mount list
.PP
List active mounts.
.SS mount status
.B mount status TARGET
.PP
Query an image or mountpoint.
.SS mount registry-path
.B mount registry-path
.PP
Report the mount registry location.
.SS unmount
.B unmount
.RI [ TARGET " | --image FILE | --mountpoint DIR"]
.PP
Unmount by image or mountpoint. Explicit selectors avoid ambiguity.
.SS unmount all
.B unmount all
.PP
Unmount all managed mounts.
.SS unmount last
.B unmount last
.PP
Unmount the most recently registered image.
.SS status
.B status
.RI [ IMAGE ]
.PP
Inspect dependencies and optionally an image's state.
.SS doctor
.B doctor
.PP
Diagnose environment and tool availability.
.SS fsck
.B fsck IMAGE
.RI [ --arg " TOKEN"]
.PP
Run dwarfsck. Repeat --arg for additional arguments.
.SS ls
.B ls IMAGE
.RI [ --path " PATH"]
.RB [ --children-only " | " --entry-only ]
.PP
List the image as path-keyed JSON. --entry-only requires --path.
.SS cat
.B cat IMAGE INNER_PATH DEST
.RB [ --force ]
.PP
Extract one file. Filename whitespace is significant. Quote paths in the shell.
A complete output is staged beside DEST. Without --force, publication refuses
existing destinations, including those created while extraction runs.
.SS peek
.B peek IMAGE
.PP
Return metadata, counts, total size and a bounded sample without mounting.
.SS usage
.B usage IMAGE
.PP
Return exact logical byte, file and directory totals plus a bounded two-level
hierarchy for visual presentation. Each level contains at most 18 entries;
smaller entries are combined into an exact Other group. The command never
attributes compressed bytes to individual paths.
.SS extract
.B extract IMAGE DEST_DIR
.RI [ --arg " TOKEN"]
.PP
Extract into a new destination directory. The command refuses an existing path,
stages the complete result beside it, and publishes only after success. Repeat
--arg for additional extraction options.
.SS checksum export
.B checksum export IMAGE --algo ALGO
.RI [ --output " FILE"]
.PP
Export checksums for files inside an image. With --output, write a staged
checksum file; otherwise return checksum text inside the JSON tool payload.
The image itself cannot be the output destination.
.SS checksum verify
.B checksum verify IMAGE --algo ALGO --input FILE
.RI [ --dir " DIR"]
.PP
Verify local files using sha256, sha512, sha1 or md5. IMAGE is context only;
this command checks extracted files, not the image bytes. Resolve FILE in the
caller's working directory. Resolve paths recorded in FILE against --dir,
or against FILE's parent directory when --dir is omitted.
.SS config show
.B config show
.RI [ --section " NAME"]
.PP
Show resolved configuration, or one section. Unknown sections are usage errors.
.SS config set
.B config set KEY VALUE [KEY VALUE ...]
.PP
Atomically update supported user preferences. Values are validated before the
user configuration is replaced.
.SS config mkdwarfs-profiles list
.B config mkdwarfs-profiles list
.RB [ --all ]
.PP
List user profiles; --all includes built-in profiles.
.SS config mkdwarfs-profiles get
.B config mkdwarfs-profiles get NAME
.PP
Read a profile's arguments.
.SS config mkdwarfs-profiles set
.B config mkdwarfs-profiles set NAME
.RI [ --arg " TOKEN"]
.PP
Store a profile. Repeat --arg for each token. Force and input/output options
are not profile settings.
.SS config mkdwarfs-profiles delete
.B config mkdwarfs-profiles delete NAME
.PP
Delete a user profile.
.SS config mkdwarfs-profiles validate
.B config mkdwarfs-profiles validate
.RI [ --arg " TOKEN"]
.PP
Validate profile arguments offline against the supported schema.
.SS mkdwarfs schema
.B mkdwarfs schema
.RB [ --include-long-help ]
.PP
Return the supported option schema and version information. Optionally include
the bundled writer option help.
.SS mkdwarfs recommend
.B mkdwarfs recommend DIR
.RI [ --goal " smallest|balanced|fastest-browse|fast-build"]
.RI [ --cache " on|off"]
.PP
Suggest flags from a bounded metadata scan; default goal balanced, cache on.
No subprocesses, content reads or compression benchmarks are performed.
The scan inspects at most 20,000 directory entries, descends through 32 levels,
and samples metadata for the first 512 regular files in sorted depth-first order.
Symlinks and special files are skipped. An oversized directory's partial
listing is discarded to avoid sampling in filesystem enumeration order.
Incomplete scans and sparse samples lower confidence.
.PP
The details schema is dwarfsctl.recommend.v1. recommendation contains
flags_only (argv tokens), reasons, warnings and confidence (low or medium).
Apply flags explicitly with build --mkdwarfs-arg, or use Auto in Dolphin's build
dialog. Recommendations do not modify profiles or start a build.
.PP
Cache on stores rule results under the user's cache directory. Every invocation
revalidates source metadata; cache hits do not avoid the bounded walk.
Cache off neither reads nor writes the recommendation cache.
.SS tools schema
.B tools schema
.PP
Report known tools and supported version metadata.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration precedence is built-in defaults, system configuration, user
configuration, then --config. Paths support environment expansion.
KDE reads resolved configuration through the backend.
.TP
.I /etc/dwarfs-dolphin/config.toml
System settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dwarfs-dolphin/config.toml
User settings; defaults to ~/.config/dwarfs-dolphin/config.toml.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME, XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Locate user settings and expand configured paths.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Session runtime storage for mounts and locks.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
State fallback when session runtime storage is unavailable.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Recommendation cache root; defaults to ~/.cache.
.TP
.B PATH
Find coreutils checksum verifiers and the FUSE unmount utility.
.TP
.B DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
Session bus used for mount control.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 generic failure; 2 invalid usage; 3 missing dependency;
4 invalid or missing path; 5 lock busy; 6 mount state error;
7 and 8 unused; 9 internal error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dwarfsctl mkdwarfs recommend ./source --goal balanced --cache off
dwarfsctl build ./source --output ./archive.dwarfs --dry-run
dwarfsctl ls ./archive.dwarfs --path /docs --children-only
dwarfsctl cat ./archive.dwarfs '/docs/note.txt' ./note.txt
dwarfsctl checksum export ./archive.dwarfs --algo sha256 --output sums
dwarfsctl checksum verify ./archive.dwarfs --algo sha256 --input sums --dir ./extracted
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
Images and the dwarfs: browser are read-only. Browser listings omit modification
times; mount the image for real filesystem timestamps. Recommendations are
metadata heuristics and cannot promise an optimal size or performance result.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkdwarfs (1),
.BR dwarfs (1),
.BR dwarfsck (1),
.BR dwarfsextract (1),
.BR sha256sum (1)

.SH NATIVE ENGINE
All image operations use a private C++ engine embedding pinned DwarFS 0.15.7.
No external DwarFS tools or Rust runtime is required. The DWARFSCTL_ENGINE
environment variable selects an explicit development engine executable.
The default engine is found in libexec beside the installation's bin directory.
